-- js-controlflow.rofl — THE THIRD LAYER, ADDED AS ONE FACT.
--
-- `layer(controlflow).` is the whole declaration, and the programme's central
-- claim is that the model then lights up every place it needs describing. That
-- claim had never been run. It was, before this file had a second line:
--
--     layer(L)                              3  ->    4
--     cell[audit](A, K, S, L)             179  ->  229
--     open_cell[audit](K, S, L)            76  ->  121
--     unqueued[audit](K, S, L)              0  ->   45
--
-- Fifty cells from one fact, forty-five of them work the plan was silent about,
-- each named by kind. Nothing had to be enumerated by hand and nothing could be
-- forgotten, which is the property the matrix exists for.
--
-- The rest of this file is the answer to what that fact enumerated.
layer(controlflow).

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- WHAT THE LAYER ANSWERS. Six kinds, and the split is by MECHANISM rather than
-- by kind — rules/js-controlflow.rofl carries the vocabulary and the audits
-- that keep it closed.
handled(js, if_statement,               controlflow, r_guard_arm).
handled(js, conditional_expression,     controlflow, r_guard_arm).
handled(js, logical_expression,         controlflow, r_guard_arm).
handled(js, for_of_statement,           controlflow, r_guard_arm).
handled(js, optional_call_expression,   controlflow, r_short_circuit).
handled(js, optional_member_expression, controlflow, r_short_circuit).

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- WHAT IT WAIVES, with the reason. `await` and `yield` transfer control and do
-- NOT guard anything: control comes back, and the code after them runs — later,
-- but it runs. This layer asks whether a site runs at all, and for a suspension
-- the answer is yes. Filing them as guards would have made `may_not_run`
-- report functions that always run.
ignored(js, await_expression, controlflow, a_control_returns_so_the_site_still_runs).
ignored(js, yield_expression, controlflow, a_control_returns_so_the_site_still_runs).

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- WHAT IT LEAVES OPEN, and it is one kind with a real question behind it.
-- Everything after a `return` in the same block is unreachable, which is a fact
-- about statement ORDER within a block — and nothing in this layer expresses
-- order at all. It is `not_yet` in the ordinary sense: real work, owned by
-- w_cf_abrupt_transfer, and `mechanism_open(abrupt, ...)` in the rules is the
-- machine-readable half of this sentence.
unknown_because(js, return_statement, controlflow, not_yet).
